module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.StrictTransformChartTorsion
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.PullbackSections.Affine
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Blowup.StrictTransformBaseChange

/-!
# The strict transform on a chart is a base change modulo torsion

`Stacks.StrictTransform.sectionsSheafEquivQuotientTorsion` computes the sections of the
sheaf-level strict transform over an affine open `V` of the base change `X ×_S S'`, on which the
inverse image of the ideal sheaf `E` is generated by a single section `a`, as the sections of
`pr_X^* F` over `V` modulo their `a`-power torsion.

The ring-level strict transform of [Stacks, Tag 053H] is a *base change* modulo `a`-power
torsion, so to compare the two the sections of `pr_X^* F` must themselves be presented as a base
change. That is what `AlgebraicGeometry.affinePullbackSectionsBaseChangeIso` does: for `U` an
affine open of `X` with `V ⊆ pr_X^{-1} U`, the sections of `pr_X^* F` over `V` are
`Γ(X ×_S S', V) ⊗_{Γ(X, U)} Γ(F, U)`. Combining the two gives the statement below, which has the
shape of the ring-level strict transform with the chart's own base-change ring in place of
`R[I/a] ⊗_R Γ(X, U)`.

What remains for the identification with the ring-level constant on the nose is the ring
comparison `Γ(X ×_S S', V) ≅ R[I/a] ⊗_R Γ(X, U)` on a blowup chart, after which
`strictTransformEquivBaseChangeQuotientTorsion`
(`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Blowup/StrictTransformBaseChange.lean`) converts the quotient below into
`strictTransform (ℐ.ideal U_S) a Γ(F, U)`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.StrictTransform.sectionsSheafEquivQuotientTorsionBaseChange`: **the comparison.** On a
  chart the sections of the strict transform of `F` are the base change
  `Γ(X ×_S S', V) ⊗_{Γ(X, U)} Γ(F, U)` modulo its `a`-power torsion.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 053H](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/053H)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 080D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/080D)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace Stacks.StrictTransform

variable {X S S' : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S) (b : S' ⟶ S) (E : S'.IdealSheafData)

/-- **The sheaf-level strict transform on a chart is a base change modulo torsion.** Let `V` be
an affine open of `X ×_S S'` on which the inverse image of `E` is generated by a single section
`a`, and `U` an affine open of `X` with `V ⊆ pr_X^{-1} U`. Then the sections of the strict
transform of a quasi-coherent module `F` over `V` are the base change
`Γ(X ×_S S', V) ⊗_{Γ(X, U)} Γ(F, U)` of the sections of `F` over `U`, modulo its `a`-power
torsion.

This is `Stacks.StrictTransform.sectionsSheafEquivQuotientTorsion` composed with
`AlgebraicGeometry.affinePullbackSectionsBaseChangeIso`; the torsion submodules correspond
because that comparison is linear over `Γ(X ×_S S', V)`, in which `a` lives. The right-hand side
is the shape of the ring-level strict transform of [Stacks, Tag 053H]. -/
def sectionsSheafEquivQuotientTorsionBaseChange (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    [QuasiCompact (exceptionalComplement f b E).ι]
    {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (V : (baseChange f b).affineOpens)
    (hVU : (V.1 : (baseChange f b).Opens) ≤ pullback.fst f b ⁻¹ᵁ U)
    (a : Γ(baseChange f b, V.1))
    (ha : (E.comap (pullback.snd f b)).ideal V = Ideal.span {a}) :
    ((ModuleCat.extendScalars ((pullback.fst f b).appLE U V.1 hVU).hom).obj
            (ModuleCat.of Γ(X, U) Γ(F, U)) ⧸
          Submodule.torsion' Γ(baseChange f b, V.1)
            ((ModuleCat.extendScalars ((pullback.fst f b).appLE U V.1 hVU).hom).obj
              (ModuleCat.of Γ(X, U) Γ(F, U)))
            (Submonoid.powers a))
        ≃ₗ[Γ(baseChange f b, V.1)] Γ(sheaf f b E F, V.1) :=
  Submodule.Quotient.equiv _ _
      (affinePullbackSectionsBaseChangeIso (pullback.fst f b) F hU V.2 hVU).toLinearEquiv
      (Submodule.map_torsion'_powers a _) ≪≫ₗ
    sectionsSheafEquivQuotientTorsion f b E F V a ha

end Stacks.StrictTransform

end
